meta {
  name: Preview Steam Library (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/user/steam/library/preview/stream
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

docs {
  SSE variant of a library preview - same event shape and caveat as
  "Import Steam Library (Stream)": a plain HTTP request just returns
  the raw event-stream body once the connection closes, not live
  progress. Emits a `progress` event per owned game considered, then
  a `done` event carrying the unlinked games as
  {steam_app_id, title, image_link} - read-only, writes nothing to the
  DB; the actual import runs through "Import Steam Library (Stream)"
  once the user has confirmed the preview. Family libraries (steam
  family IDs on the account) are merged in.

  503 if neither the caller nor the server has a Steam Web API key
  configured - a real top-level HTTP response, raised before the SSE
  stream opens. A missing Steam ID, by contrast, surfaces as an
  `error` event inside an HTTP 200 stream.
}